cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use fhirground in published work, please cite it as below."
title: "fhirground: grounded, validated FHIR R4 extraction from clinical notes"
abstract: >-
  fhirground splits notes-to-FHIR extraction in two. Schema-constrained LLM
  decoding produces simple, plain-language mentions, each with a verbatim
  evidence quote and an assertion status; deterministic, tested code then
  grounds each mention to character offsets, resolves codes through a pluggable
  terminology layer, maps mentions to FHIR R4 Condition, MedicationRequest, and
  Observation resources, validates them, and attaches per-resource confidence
  and evidence extensions. The mention schema contains no code fields, so a
  model cannot emit a medical code; every coding in the output comes from a
  terminology resolver, enforced structurally and checked by a property test.
type: software
